  "authors": [],
  "body": {
    "comment": "I support setting the Net-Change-Limit (NCL) for 2025 at 350 000 000 000 000 lovelace (₳350 million), roughly reflecting the Treasury inflows recorded in 2024.\n\nOver the longer term, the NCL should be implemented as a protocol parameter and defined as a percentage of the live Treasury balance rather than a fixed number. A percentage-based guardrail would scale automatically, enabling smoother withdrawals and preventing a scenario where a large, fixed cap, potentially hundreds of millions of ada, could be withdrawn in a single action once a Treasury withdrawal governance proposal is approved."
  },
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256"
}